# Validation of the Julia Runtime Environment (Project 1)

**Architects:** Wieland Hoffmann (Human Core), Gemini (Machine Core), Grok (xAI)  
**System:** Intel i9, cores 2–15 isolated, OS on cores 0–1  
**Status:** Experimental measurement runs, protection rights pending

## 15-Minute Multithreading Run

In a 15-minute parallel run across 14 threads, 9,794 cycles were completed. The cycle rate per minute ranged from approximately 590 to 700. CPU temperature stayed between 49 °C and 64 °C. System fans remained at 0 RPM in the documented run. SSD temperature was 33.9 °C.

## Numerical Stress Tests

The plasma simulation was run with increasing disturbance force. Up to step 280 the confinement remained stable in the documented run. At higher disturbance force floating-point overflows and numerical instabilities occurred (documented from step 320 onward).

The results refer to the tested hardware, the Julia version and the parameters used. They describe the behavior of the isolated cores under the documented conditions and do not constitute a general claim of numerical stability or jitter-free operation under all load conditions.

